  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of labour migration and mobility in line with ILS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports Lebanon in strengthening fair and effective labour migration governance and promoting decent work in the care economy, with a focus on better protection of migrant workers, refugees and domestic workers. In a context of political and economic fragility, weak enforcement capacity and heightened risks of exploitation, the intervention supports tripartite constituents to establish or strengthen institutional mechanisms for implementing and monitoring labour migration governance frameworks, while advancing policy and legislative reform in line with international labour standards and ILO guidance on fair recruitment, refugee access to labour markets and decent work in care.

The strategy combines evidence-based policy advice, research, capacity building, social dialogue and the promotion of good practices. It will strengthen the capacity of government, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations to design and implement measures that improve protection, access to services and decent work outcomes for migrant and domestic workers. In collaboration with trade unions and other non-state actors, the ILO will support case documentation, referrals, administrative and legal assistance, community-based outreach, and cross-border coordination through existing trade union cooperation arrangements with countries of origin. The intervention will also generate evidence on systemic gaps to inform advocacy and medium- to long-term policy solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
